  "question": {
    "text": "Two tangent galvanometers A and B have coils of radii 8 cm and 16 cm respectively and resistance <math><mn>8</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&Omega;</mi></math> each. They are connected in parallel with a cell of emf 4 V and negligible internal resistance. The deflections produced in the tangent galvanometers A and B are <math><mn>30</mn><mo>&deg;</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&deg;</mo></math> respectively. If A has 2 turns, then B must have",
